 result←object Print arg;dr;NL;FF;position;t;line;tunits;page;fs;pagesize;NeverSuppress;dirty;fontdefn;units
 '∆WI ARGUMENT ERROR: Argument required for "Print" method'##.##.Error 0=≢arg
 '∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Print'##.##.Error 1≠≢arg
 '∆WI RANK ERROR: Print'##.##.Error 1<≢⍴arg←⊃arg
 '∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Print'##.##.Error~0 1∊⍨≡arg
 (tunits units)←1 0 1/##._supp.MyUnits object ⍝ Will provide printer-specific values

 ⍝ Make sure we have a reasonable font to use
 :If 0=≢fontdefn←object ⎕VGET⊂'_font' '' ⍝ Have they defined a global font for this printer?
     ⍝ If not, we'll have to invent our own temporary font (to be removed later)
     {}object ##.font 'Courier New'(units÷⍥⊃tunits) ⍝ Default font size = 1 character printer-unit tall (regardless of scale)
⍝? Problem: Every printer seems to have a different default font - how can we tell them apart?
 :EndIf

 :If 0=object._opened ⍝ If the Printer is currently closed, we need to Open it first
     object('Open'##.##.Invoke)⍬
 :EndIf

 ⍝ Clean up the argument
 :If ##.##.IsChar arg←,arg ⍝ The usual case
     ⍝ We should be able to print this as-is
 :ElseIf ##.##.IsInt arg
     'DOMAIN ERROR: Unicode values out of range'##.##.Error∨/~(0∘≤∧≤∘65535)arg
     arg←⎕UCS⌊0.5+arg ⍝ Convert this whole thing to text first
 :ElseIf ∧/0 1 2 3 5∊⍨dr←10|⎕DR¨arg ⍝ Check if it's mixed text and numbers
     'DOMAIN ERROR: Unicode values out of range'##.##.Error∨/~(0∘≤∧≤∘65535)(dr∊1 3 5)/arg
     arg←{⎕UCS⌊0.5+⍵}@(⍸dr∊1 3 5)⊢arg ⍝ Convert only the numbers to text
 :Else
     ##.##.Error'∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Print'
 :EndIf

 ⍝ Now we should have a simple character vector to process
 (NL FF)←⎕UCS 13 12 ⋄ dirty←0
 (pagesize position page)←object ⎕VGET('_size'⍬)('_position'(0 0))('_page' 0)
 pagesize×←tunits ⍝ For use when comparing to position
 :While ×≢arg
     :Select ⊃arg
     :Case NL
         position←2↑position[1]+tunits[1]×⊃object ##._supp.GetTextSize'X' ⍝ Move to the beginning of the next line
         arg←1↓arg
     :Case FF
         :If object dirty ⍬ ⍝ Don't auto-eject if the page is not yet dirty
             2 ##.##.∆NQ object'NewPage'
             page+←1 ⋄ position←0 0
             'Page'##.##.Event object ##.##.Application page
         :EndIf
         arg←1↓arg
     :Else
         line←(t←¯1+⌊/arg⍳NL,FF)↑arg ⋄ arg←t↓arg
         fs←tunits×object ##._supp.GetTextSize line
         :If (position[1]>0)∧⊃pagesize<position+fs ⍝ If this will overflow the page vertically, eject first
             2 ##.##.∆NQ object'NewPage'
             page+←1 ⋄ position←0 0
             'Page'##.##.Event object ##.##.Application page
         :EndIf
         (object._pic⍕⍛,'.')##.##.∆WC'Text'('Coord' 'RealPixel')('Text'line)('Points'position)
         page⌈←1 ⋄ position[2]+←fs[2] ⋄ dirty←1
     :EndSelect
 :EndWhile
 object._position←position ⋄ object._page←page
 :If dirty∧~object._dirty ⋄ object._dirty←1 ⋄ object ##.##.∆WS⊂'Dirty' 1 ⋄ :EndIf
 :If 0=≢fontdefn ⋄ {}object ##.font,⊂fontdefn ⋄ object._font←fontdefn ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Restore original default font setting if we invented one

 result←##.NoRes
